### 1.5 Implementation Details

#### A. Modify Exit Icon Handler ([`AttendanceScreen.kt:1307`](file:///c:/Users/amitk/OneDrive/Documents/ChatGPT/Attract%20-%20Face%20Based%20Attendance%20Tracker/app/src/main/java/com/attract/attendance/feature/attendance/AttendanceScreen.kt#L1307))

**Current:**
```kotlin
IconButton(onClick = { showPinDialog = true }) { ... }
```

**New:**
```kotlin
IconButton(onClick = { launchFingerprintAuth() }) { ... }
```

Where `launchFingerprintAuth()` is a function that:
1. Checks if biometric is available via `BiometricManager.canAuthenticate(BIOMETRIC_STRONG)`
2. If available → show `BiometricPrompt` with:
   - Title: `"Teacher Verification"`
   - Subtitle: `"Scan your fingerprint to end session"`
   - Negative button: `"Use PIN Instead"`
3. If NOT available (no hardware or not enrolled) → fall directly to `showPinDialog = true`

#### B. BiometricPrompt Callbacks

```kotlin
val biometricPrompt = BiometricPrompt(activity, executor, object : AuthenticationCallback() {
    override fun onAuthenticationSucceeded(result: AuthenticationResult) {
        // ✅ Fingerprint verified → unpin + end session
        scope.launch {
            lockTaskController?.stop()
            isScreenPinned = false
            if (presentIds.isEmpty()) {
                showZeroConfirmDialog = true
            } else {
                onEndSession(presentIds)
            }
        }
    }

    override fun onAuthenticationError(errorCode: Int, errString: CharSequence) {
        when (errorCode) {
            ERROR_LOCKOUT, ERROR_LOCKOUT_PERMANENT -> {
                // 3+ failures → auto-show PIN dialog
                showPinDialog = true
            }
            ERROR_NEGATIVE_BUTTON -> {
                // User tapped "Use PIN Instead"
                showPinDialog = true
            }
            ERROR_USER_CANCELED -> {
                // User cancelled → do nothing, stay on screen
            }
        }
    }

    override fun onAuthenticationFailed() {
        // System shows "Not recognized. Try again." automatically
        // No action needed — system handles retry counter
    }
})
```

> [!NOTE]
> The system `BiometricPrompt` already handles:
> - The fingerprint animation and scanning UI (beautiful system dialog)
> - "Not recognized. Try again." retry message
> - Automatic lockout after 3-5 failed attempts (triggers `ERROR_LOCKOUT`)
> - There is no need for a custom fingerprint UI — the system dialog is premium and consistent across Android devices.

